  "id": "DrugBank_DB11799 - MONDO_5109",
  "verbalization": "Bictegravir is implicated in the treatment of HIV infectious disease through a chain of indications that ultimately lead to its association with this condition. The evidence suggests that Bictegravir is used in the management of AIDS, which in turn is linked to HIV infectious disease. This pathway is supported by the indication of Bictegravir for AIDS, and the subsequent indications for Zalcitabine and Tenofovir Disoproxil, both of which are known to be used in the treatment of HIV. The integration of these indications implies that Bictegravir may play a role in the treatment of HIV infectious disease through its use in managing AIDS. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, highlighting a potential mechanism by which Bictegravir contributes to the treatment of HIV infectious disease.",
